      "id": 1,
      "text": "The First Congregational Church on Hillside Road, founded by English Puritan descendants in 1740, is Chester’s oldest standing building.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://westfieldnj.com/whs/history/chesterboro.htm",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Chester’s railroad, opened in 1869, once hauled ore from local mines to market, shaping the borough’s early industrial boom.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://westfieldnj.com/whs/history/chesterboro.htm",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Chester Library’s Local History Department now hosts 392 digitized images of historic Chester, making the past accessible online.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://localhistory.chesterlib.org/",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Many 1800‑s structures in Historic Main Street survive today as restaurants, galleries, and shops, preserving Chester’s architectural heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://westfieldnj.com/whs/history/chesterboro.htm",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Before European settlement, the Lenni‑Lenape Indians arrived from eastern Long Island in the 1730s, founding the area that became Chester.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
